    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d896">

                <pb facs="0900" n="888" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg888"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">856D.6176/391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-16T13:00:00+00:00">February 16, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 16—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. Department’s 43, February 11, 2 p.m. I called upon Lord Halifax, the Acting
                    Foreign Secretary, this morning and in delivering the note<anchor n="21"
                        xml:id="d896-f1"/> took occasion to outline the American position.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
